[materialization-audit]
The first partial-tree run stopped before sync-wrapper logic because scripts/sync.sh
had been materialized without its Git mode=100755 executable bit:
  tests/test_sync_wrapper_signal.sh: .../scripts/sync.sh: Permission denied
The repository tree was queried and confirmed launch.sh and sync.sh are both 100755.
Restoring those exact modes made lifecycle, wrapper-signal and zombie-lock pass.

The next partial-tree run stopped before sync-worker logic because core/kap_core.h,
then native/sync.c, were absent from the transient local subset. Both were restored
from their exact Git blobs and independently verified with git hash-object. No source
or test expectation was changed to address either materialization defect.

